### HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# 1. Install the VS Code extension "REST Client" (by Huachao Mao)
# 2. A small "Send Request" link appears above each request — click it
# 3. The response (status, headers, body) opens on the right
# Requests are separated by ###

@base = https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com

### 1. GET one resource (path parameter)
GET {{base}}/posts/1

### 2. GET a list
GET {{base}}/users

### 3. GET with query parameters (filter)
GET {{base}}/posts?userId=1

### 4. GET something that doesn't exist → expect 404
GET {{base}}/posts/99999

### 5. HEAD — headers only, no body
HEAD {{base}}/posts/1

### 6. POST — create (look at the status: 201, not 200)
POST {{base}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learning HTTP",
  "body": "My first POST request",
  "userId": 1
}

### 7. PUT — replace the whole resource
PUT {{base}}/posts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Replaced",
  "body": "Everything is replaced",
  "userId": 1
}

### 8. PATCH — change only one field
PATCH {{base}}/posts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Only the title changed"
}

### 9. DELETE
DELETE {{base}}/posts/1

### 10. Nested resource: comments of post 1
GET {{base}}/posts/1/comments

### 11. See your own request echoed back (headers, query, body)
POST https://httpbin.org/anything?lesson=1
Content-Type: application/json
X-My-Header: hello

{ "learning": "http" }

### 12. Ask for a specific status code
GET https://httpbin.org/status/418

### 13. Authorization header (httpbin checks it)
GET https://httpbin.org/bearer
Authorization: Bearer my-fake-token

### 14. Same endpoint WITHOUT a token → expect 401
GET https://httpbin.org/bearer
